      "content": "Assessing the **Trans-Pacific Partnership (TPP, now CPTPP for the remaining members) for the domestic working class is highly contested and complex, with evidence supporting both sides of the argument. Proponents argue that the increased trade and lower tariffs created more high-skill, higher-wage job opportunities in certain sectors, leading to overall economic growth. However, strong criticisms point to the acceleration of manufacturing decline in certain domestic industries due to intense competition, sometimes leading to wage stagnation and job displacement for the less-skilled or in specific, targeted sectors.",
